  "title": "Her New Husband Left Her at the Train Station After the Wedding: \"You Don't Belong in My World\"",
  "description": "The morning after her wedding, Ivy stepped off the train in Chicago alone — her purse, her phone and her mother&apos;s ring gone, and a letter in her hand: &quot;You don&apos;t belong in my world.&quot;<br><br>Brett Mercer married Ivy Calloway for her uncle&apos;s money, took everything she had on the train, and walked away. She didn&apos;t know a single person in the city. Then a café owner named Maggie ran across the street with a broom, chased off two men grabbing her last suitcase, and gave her a job and a room upstairs. Ivy started over, brewing her mother&apos;s apple cinnamon tea for a regular named Adrian — until his aunt walked in with a $50,000 check and told her to leave town.<br><br>Weeks later, Ivy was pouring tea at the Cole Hotel Group gala when Brett walked in with a new girlfriend on his arm and laughed at her in front of everyone. Then the lights went down, the big screen lit up, and Ivy saw her mother&apos;s apple orchard — sold for a lakeside resort. Brett found the buyer. And the consent on that contract carries her own signature, signed the morning of her wedding.<br><br>👉 Watch till the end — the girl he called &quot;not from my world&quot; is about to show him exactly where she belongs.<br><br>If you love stories where the underdog stands up and the liars get caught, subscribe for a new story every week.<br><br>This is a fictional story made for entertainment. All characters, places and events are invented.<br><br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/dramastory\">#DramaStory</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/revenge\">#Revenge</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/story\">#Story</a>",
